Track 1: Loom-Pipes Unpick the Bedrock
- Story & Context: When a cage cable snapped during a shift change at the Boulby Potash Basin, grease-monkey Devraj Sen found himself entombed in total darkness smelling of sulfurous damp alongside five Leeds fitters. To ward off the paralyzing cold and creeping carbon monoxide, Devraj grabbed a twelve-pound spanner and began hammering a frantic, swinging garage pattern against the hollow secondary air conduit, screaming over the ringing zinc: "We pull the thread until the rock gives in." Within an hour, the men were clapping syncopated grime rhythms against their hardhats while Devraj laced classical Todi melodic turns into the intake valve's metallic howling. When the rescue crew finally breached the rockfall three days later, they discovered the crew entirely uninjured, dancing in exhaustion to the acoustic slipstream of their homemade industrial loom.
