Track 2: "Did You Mend the Air-Line?"
- Story & Context: In the cramped surface barracks of Shaft Four, rhythm guitarist Michelle "Mitch" Vane spent her off-shift hours running her customized Telecaster through an open flanger circuit grounded to the room's radiator pipes. Heartbroken over the quiet departure of her longtime lover—a drill operator who fled the pits without saying goodbye—she channeled her insomnia into staccato, syncopated skanks that mimicked the dying sputter of subterranean oxygen scrubbers. Over a bruising 138-BPM breakbeat built from bootleg field recordings of pressure releases, she leaned close to the guitar pickups and muttered: "You left the valve wide open and the cold got in." The track leaked onto underground pirate radio networks, quickly becoming the unofficial anthem for shift workers nursing unspoken losses in the deep dark.
